                <pb facs="0774" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg680"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    your note, dated the 12th instant, relative to the inscription of citizens of
                    the United States in the municipal offices of the Island of Cuba, and I must
                    state to you in reply that I have hastened to communicate the contents of the
                    aforesaid note to the Governor-General of the island, and I am sure that that
                    authority will appreciate the attitude of the Government of the United States,
                    and will give the orders which are desired.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
